# WikiRace Design System

## Personality
Clean, editorial, and energetic. Feels like a premium product, not a generic AI-generated app. Warm and inviting — players should feel happy visiting. Never: purple gradients, generic card stacks, or default system fonts.

## Fonts (loaded via Google Fonts in index.css)
- **Logo/brand**: `Bebas Neue` — used only for the "WikiRace" wordmark
- **Article titles & challenge names**: `DM Serif Display` — serif, editorial, makes article names feel important
- **All UI text**: `DM Sans` — clean, modern, readable

```css
font-family: var(--font-display);  /* Bebas Neue */
font-family: var(--font-serif);    /* DM Serif Display */
font-family: var(--font-sans);     /* DM Sans */
```

## Color palette (CSS variables in index.css)
```css
--bg: #F8F7F4           /* warm off-white — page background */
--surface: #FFFFFF       /* cards, modals, article area */
--surface-muted: #F3F2EF /* subtle backgrounds inside surfaces */
--bar-bg: #18181B        /* game bar — near black */
--bar-border: #2D2D31
--text: #18181B
--text-muted: #71717A
--text-faint: #A1A1AA
--accent: #D63E1F        /* warm red — CTAs, highlights */
--accent-hover: #B83319
--accent-light: #FEF0EC
--link: #1D4ED8          /* Wikipedia-style blue for clickable links */
--link-hover: #1E3FAD
--border: #E4E4E7
--border-strong: #D4D4D8
--green: #16A34A         /* success / win state */
--green-light: #DCFCE7
```

## Spacing & shape
- Border radius: `--radius: 10px`, `--radius-sm: 6px`, `--radius-lg: 16px`
- Max content width: **750px** (article), **860px** (game bar)
- Shadows: `--shadow-sm`, `--shadow`, `--shadow-lg` — subtle, never heavy

## UI conventions
- Primary CTA buttons: `background: var(--accent)`, white text, `box-shadow` with red tint, hover lifts with `translateY(-1px)`
- Secondary/ghost buttons: `border: 1px solid var(--border)`, muted text, no fill
- Section labels: `0.7rem`, `700` weight, `0.12em` letter-spacing, uppercase, `var(--text-faint)` color
- Modals/dialogs: `border-radius: var(--radius-lg)`, `box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg)`, fade+slide-down animation
- Loading states: animated progress bar using `--accent`, never a full-page spinner blocking content
- Error states: `#FEF2F2` background, `#FECACA` border, `#B91C1C` text

## Animations
Use these keyframes (defined in index.css):
- `fadeIn` — opacity + translateY(8px), for screen transitions and modals
- `slideDown` — for dropdowns and dialogs
- `spin` — for the loading spinner
- Keep transitions at `0.15s–0.2s ease` for snappiness

## Responsive
- Mobile-first thinking. Minimum touch target: 44px.
- On mobile: infoboxes and floated images become block-level (handled in article.css)
- Game bar stays sticky and readable at all widths

## Don't do
- Don't add new fonts without removing one — keep it to 3 families max
- Don't use purple, blue gradients, or glassmorphism
- Don't add heavy UI libraries (no Tailwind, no MUI, no Chakra)
- Don't break the warm/editorial aesthetic with neon or overly playful elements
